Subject: wireless/bcmf: propagate gSPI register errors and preserve the worker

Register accessors previously returned uninitialized or partial DMA data and
reported writes as successful regardless of the backend result. Return a
checked status and commit register outputs and cached power state only on
success. Keep an interrupt pending until its read and acknowledgement succeed.

Use the same checked status path with diagnostics enabled or disabled. Unknown
status never authorizes receive/transmit work. Retain bounded Bluetooth service
and wait between failed polls; do not enter an indefinite low-power wait after
a failed transition. Recovery requests bypass a stale cached power state.

A zero-length F2 record is malformed receive input, not a shutdown request:
flush it using the existing receive recovery path without exiting the shared
Wi-Fi/Bluetooth worker. No application deadline or radio setting is changed.

